# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Inzozi Motors — website (web/)
# Copy to .env.local for development. Never commit the filled-in file.
#
# There are two API URLs on purpose, and they are usually different values.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Server-side only. This is the address the Next server itself uses to reach the
# backend when it renders a page — Server Components, Server Actions, route
# handlers. It never reaches the browser, so it can be a private address:
#   Docker Compose : http://api:3000        (the service name on the bridge net)
#   Same VPS       : http://127.0.0.1:3000  (never leaves the machine)
#   Local dev      : http://localhost:3000
API_URL=http://localhost:3000

# Public. Inlined into the browser bundle at build time, so it must be an
# address a PHONE ON MOBILE DATA can reach — never an internal Docker host.
#   Production : https://api.inzozimotors.rw
#   Local dev  : http://localhost:3000
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:3000

# Public. The site's own canonical origin. Used for metadataBase, canonical
# URLs, the sitemap, robots.txt and the Open Graph card, so a wrong value here
# silently poisons every shared link.
#   Production : https://inzozimotors.rw
#   Local dev  : http://localhost:3002
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3002

# Port the standalone server listens on. 3000 is the API and 3001 is the admin
# dashboard, so the website takes 3002.
PORT=3002
